  "details": "nginx is a web and proxy server supporting HTTP and other protocols, with a focus on high concurrency, performance, and low memory usage.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * nginx: nginx: heap-based buffer overflow in ngx_http_core_module via alias with rewrite referencing $request_filename (CVE-2026-15176)\n  * nginx: NGINX ngx_http_core_module vulnerability (CVE-2026-97205)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
